{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"THIRD DEFECT — ssh-keygen is not in the review-bot image. This was the actual blocker.\n\nAfter change 89128b2e09 deployed (identity + key mount), I exercised the REAL signing seam\nin-process inside the container rather than trusting the config state. Everything looked\nright and it STILL did not sign:\n\n  cfg signing_key : /run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key\n  env var         : /run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key\n  key readable    : True\n  author          : Rebar Bot\n  author_email    : joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com\n  author_id       : 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\n  author_sig      : ABSENT\n  SIGN RAISED     : SshKeygenUnavailable — ssh-keygen (OpenSSH) not found;\n                    SSHSIG requires OpenSSH >= 8.9\n\nrebar signs authorship with SSHSIG via `ssh-keygen -Y sign` (rebar.attest.sshsig). The\nreview-bot image is FROM python:3.12-slim installing only `git curl ca-certificates`, so\nssh-keygen was never present. sign_event_authorship raises, _seam catches it, event written\nunsigned.\n\nWHY IT STAYED HIDDEN FOR A MONTH: the exception is only logged as a WARNING, and it was never\neven reached while author_id was null — _seam gates on `if author_id and signing_key`, so\ndefect 1 short-circuited before the try block. Fixing the identity is what let this surface.\nThat is also why config-level verification was insufficient: every observable input was\ncorrect and the output was still unsigned.\n\nFIX PUSHED — Gerrit change 1570: add openssh-client to Dockerfile.reviewbot (Debian bookworm\nships OpenSSH 9.2, clearing the 8.9 floor) + a static guard test asserting the image installs\nit, verified RED then GREEN. Dockerfile.reviewbot is in autodeploy's BOT_PATHS, so submitting\nrebuilds the image on the box.\n\nFULL CAUSAL CHAIN (all three had to be fixed; any one alone leaves events unsigned):\n  1. no global git identity  -> author_id null -> signing skipped silently   [89128b2e09]\n  2. key not mounted         -> host path unreadable in container            [89128b2e09]\n  3. ssh-keygen absent       -> SSHSIG raises -> caught -> unsigned          [1570]"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786305904158605001,"uuid":"ef86ec55-a93e-4da7-b1f3-98430c3278c0"}